    "implementation_delta": "Publish AcceleratePythonExternalClient@1 as the Accelerate-owned hermetic Python client against the same canonical service MCP and CLI would use. The client submits the PCPR-060 canonical objective bytes, receives objective CID baguqeeraynsn7tjr3iaggnreylzxo3akaooqwp5bf5oheaa6eubth2zwqeba, subscribes to events, inspects task state, submits candidate evidence, and retrieves PCPR-072 chain CID baguqeeraeuvfodvledfa4nvfuso6eyyytzk2acptcogzwzyarkdinpqcsdfq. The Python principal principal:pcpr-080-python-external-client is intent, never authority. Forbidden client operations including task mutation, terminalization, policy forgery, confirmation/lease/fence bypass, scope broadening, current-root writes, and self-promotion are refused. DatasetsPythonExternalClientBinding@1 and KitPythonExternalClientBinding@1 consume the Accelerate client without reminting pack, current-root, chain, objective, or protocol identities. Replaying the same client command yields client CID baguqeerat346yf4k7kenbqlbtyejeilgxamna262z3axzjjatzm2hccehblq and is rejected as a duplicate effect. Live Supervisor.run, live Quack, live MCP, and live CLI stay typed unavailable. Missing a live Quack-fenced session emits operator-blocking task pcpr-080-operator-live-python-external-client. Generic MCP-client demonstration remains PCPR-081. This evaluator never writes DuckDB or Quack state and never emits a closed PCPR release outcome."
  },
